course: dictionary
lesson: 7195
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word pet has more than one meaning, so the context tells you which one you need. «A pet needs food, water, care, exercise and time every day: it is a responsibility, not a toy.» Here a pet is an animal that lives with people at home.
explain: Context can also show you a different meaning. In Newcastle «pet» is a friendly word like «love», as in «howay» meaning «come on». Nobody there means a cat or a dog when they say it, so read the clues around the word before you decide.
explain: Ask the context question: what would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence. If «an animal kept at home» makes sense, you have found the meaning. If it does not, look for a clue that points to a different meaning.
fact: A pet is an animal that lives with people at home and is cared for.
fact: To pet an animal means to stroke it gently.
fact: A teacher's pet is a pupil the teacher seems to like best.
fact: «Pet tortoises» often live 50 years, and Jonathan, a giant tortoise on St Helena, is reported to be around 190 years old.
fact: Pet can also be a friendly word in some parts of England, and a pet hate is something you dislike more than anything else.
exercise: «A pet needs food, water, care, exercise and time every day.» What is a pet in this sentence? | *An animal that lives with people and is cared for | A place where animals sleep | A toy that needs no care
exercise: Sam says, «Please pet the dog gently.» What does pet mean here? | To buy at a shop | *To stroke gently | To feed in a bowl | To hit hard
exercise: «She is the teacher's pet, so she is always picked first.» What does teacher's pet mean? | A pet who lives in the classroom | A pupil who is always late | A teacher who keeps animals | *A pupil the teacher seems to like best
test: In Newcastle, «howay» means «come on» and «pet» is a friendly word like «love». What does pet mean in «Howay, pet»? | To stroke gently | A small animal | A pupil the teacher likes | *A friendly word, like love
test: Mia says, «Long division is my pet hate.» What does pet hate mean? | *Something you dislike most, your own special dislike | A hamster you keep in class | A kind of food for pets | Something you love most
exam: Which use of pet means an animal kept at home? | Pet, come here now | My pet hate is spiders | To pet a rabbit is kind | *«Pet tortoises often live 50 years»
